---
title: OpsNow — Roles & Access Model (Cumulative)
---
flowchart LR
    classDef note fill:#FEF3C7,stroke:#D97706,text-align:left

    subgraph EMP["EMPLOYEE — baseline"]
        direction TB
        E1["Create & view own<br/>tickets, add comments"]
        E2["View assets currently<br/>assigned to them"]
        E3["Read published<br/>knowledge base articles"]
    end

    subgraph SA["+ SUPPORT AGENT"]
        direction TB
        S1["View & triage ALL tickets,<br/>assign, change status/priority"]
        S2["Internal notes &<br/>full ticket history"]
        S3["Manage assets:<br/>assign, return, track"]
        S4["Author knowledge<br/>base articles"]
        S5["SLA dashboard &<br/>AI assistant panel"]
    end

    subgraph TL["+ TEAM LEAD"]
        direction TB
        T1["Agent performance<br/>analytics (per-person)"]
    end

    subgraph ADM["+ ADMINISTRATOR"]
        direction TB
        A1["User directory<br/>(GET /users)"]
        A2["Audit log<br/>(append-only trail)"]
    end

    NOTE["Effective access is cumulative because each role's route list<br/>is a superset of the previous role's — not a coded inheritance<br/>chain. Authorization is layered: RolesGuard enforces route-level<br/>role requirements where a route declares them, while service-level<br/>visibility/ownership/business-rule checks independently constrain<br/>every route's data — the frontend's role-aware UI is a convenience<br/>layer, never the security boundary."]:::note

    EMP --> SA --> TL --> ADM --> NOTE
